# Copy to `.env.local`, either beside a project's AGENT.md or in the directory you
# run coauthor from.
#
# Precedence, most specific first:
#   1. <project>/.env.local   this project's own model and proxy
#   2. <cwd>/.env.local       a fallback, so one credential serves every project
#   3. the shell environment
#
# Both files beat the shell, so a variable exported for another tool cannot defeat a
# project's own configuration. Keeping only a token in the cwd file and letting each
# project pin its model is the arrangement with the fewest copies of the secret.
# `.env.local` is gitignored; this example file is not, so keep real tokens out of it.
#
# coauthor reads COAUTHOR_* only. An ANTHROPIC_* variable in your shell is ignored,
# so a proxy or model exported for another tool cannot redirect this project.
# `coauthor check` lists any it finds.

# Credential. COAUTHOR_AUTH_TOKEN is checked first, then COAUTHOR_API_KEY.
COAUTHOR_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional: an Anthropic-compatible proxy. Omit for the official API.
# COAUTHOR_BASE_URL=https://apiproxy.example.com

# Optional: defaults to claude-sonnet-4-6. Any model the base URL serves.
# COAUTHOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Optional: response cap per model call. Defaults to 8192. Raise it if a long
# chapter gets truncated mid-sentence.
# COAUTHOR_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# Optional: extended-thinking strength. Defaults to off so Anthropic-compatible
# proxies that reject the thinking field keep working. Values: off, low, medium,
# high. The corresponding budget is clamped when max tokens is too small.
# COAUTHOR_EFFORT=off
